# quality.yaml reference

`quality.yaml` sits at the repository root. It is optional: without it, every check runs advisory with defaults. `qk` validates it against `plugins/quality-kit/schemas/quality.schema.json` (rule QK001).

| Key | Value | Description |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `version` | `1`; required | Schema version. |
| `maturity` | `bronze`, `silver` or `gold`; default `bronze` | How strict the repo is. |
| `modes` | map of check key to `off`, `advisory` or `enforced` | Mode \| per check. |
| `docs` | object | Where docs live. |
| `docs.root` | string; default `docs` | Docs folder. |
| `docs.diataxis` | `true` or `false` | Use Diátaxis folders. |
| `docs.impact_map` | list of objects | Code paths mapped to docs. |
| `docs.impact_map[].paths` | list of strings; required | Code globs. |
